{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said.</b> Moses, corresponding to all Israel — and the meaning is that he says thus to Israel." "And the meaning of \"my commandments\" — concerning the people who left over of it until morning." "And the meaning of \"and my Torah\" — that HaShem taught them the reason for the Sabbath; therefore they gathered a double portion of bread. And the reason for the plural form, \"my commandments and my Torah\": for all the commandments and Torahs are truth without doubt, according to their plain sense, and they have secrets in matters of the soul, and none understand them except the discerning. Therefore every commandment is two."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:11.011575314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}